midifreaq lets you find the MIDI note for the provided frequency or inversely let's you find the frequency of the provided MIDI note

# Usage
1. Download the repo & type make in your terminal
2. Move the executable out of the build directory to desired location

./midifreaq [options] rootFreq freq/midinote octaveDivision

Options:
  - -h: Show documentation
  - -m: Find midinote closest to frequency
  - -f: Find frequency of midinote

Pick one flag(-m or -f) & then enter a root frequency(Greater than 0) in the rootFreq position.

Enter either a frequency in Hz or a MIDI note in the freq/midinote position.

Enter an octave division higher than 5 in the octaveDivision position.

Examples:
./midifreaq -f 440 261.63 12
./midifreaq -m 440 60 12